changetrack-ng (0.5.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Perf: status, diff, and log subcommands now apply the metadata fast-path,
    skipping unchanged files without spawning a VCS process per file.
  * Add t/16-subcommands.t: coverage for status/diff fast-path and clean-file diff_path.

 -- Christopher Cashell <topher@zyp.org>  Fri, 08 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

changetrack-ng (0.5.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: all unattended invocations (apt, pacman hooks; cron; systemd service) now
    pass --quiet, preventing change reports from flooding terminal output during
    package manager operations. DNF plugin was already fully silent.

 -- Christopher Cashell <topher@zyp.org>  Tue, 06 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

changetrack-ng (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add config_keys() to each notifier; Runner::_build_notifier filters args
    to only the keys the target notifier accepts. Surfaces missing webhook_timeout.
  * Add t/21-report.t: 52-test dedicated suite for ChangeTrack::Report.
  * Add missing start_time/end_time accessors to Report.pm.
  * Fix: MockSendmail $VERSION now derived from ChangeTrack::Version.
  * Perf: cache /etc/machine-id in OTLP::_resource_attrs() via state variable.
  * Perf: pass pre-computed mode to _resolve_sensitive(); eliminates redundant stat().
  * Fix: webhook diff counters no longer count unified diff +++ / --- header lines.
  * Fix: eliminate redundant $vcs->add() call after checkin() in Runner.
  * Fix: Fossil/SVN chdir() wrapped in exception-safe eval; Mercurial uses -R.
  * Add: --dry-run / -n flag for static change analysis without VCS mutation.
  * Precompile ignore patterns once per run (was per-file); improves scaling.
  * Deduplicate notifier construction via shared _build_notifier helper.

 -- Christopher Cashell <topher@zyp.org>  Tue, 06 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

changetrack-ng (0.4.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Unified metadata type system: drop skip_reason, use single type field
    (file, symlink, binary, empty, unreadable, special, directory, missing).
  * Performance: metadata-based fast path skips unchanged files without I/O.
  * Fix: symlinks no longer misclassified as binary.
  * Fix: empty (zero-byte) files no longer flagged as binary.
  * Fix: binary file warnings only emitted on first detection.
  * Fix: getpwuid/getgrgid portability for non-POSIX platforms.

 -- Christopher Cashell <topher@zyp.org>  Sun, 04 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

changetrack-ng (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging.
  * Clean Perl rewrite of changetrack with modern VCS and notification support.
  * Supports RCS, Git, Fossil, SVN, Mercurial VCS backends.
  * Supports Email, Webhook, OTLP, and File notification channels.
  * Includes systemd timer, cron.hourly script, and apt/pacman hooks.

 -- Christopher Cashell <topher@zyp.org>  Mon, 28 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
